 "name": "well",
 "archetype": "prop.well",
 "description": "A village draw well: a round wall of staggered stone blocks on a mortar core with a plinth and a coping ring, a dark shaft with water a little below the rim, two timber posts with feet and knee braces carrying a ridge beam and a shingled gable roof with barge boards, and a windlass (winch) between the posts with an iron axle, rope coil and crank handle that turns about x, plus a hooped wooden bucket on its rope.",
